<KaburioPolicyLayout lang="en" legacy>
  <p>This page describes older builds with ads (versionCode 2 and earlier). The current policy applies to the new ad-free build.</p>
  <section aria-labelledby="section-1">
    <h2 id="section-1">1. Operator and app</h2>
    <p>TATTO LAB (the “Operator”) provides KABURIO for Android, package name com.tattolab.kaburio. This policy explains how information is handled in the app.</p>
    <p>Contact: <a href="mailto:tattoqq9@gmail.com">tattoqq9@gmail.com</a></p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="section-2">
    <h2 id="section-2">2. Photos, videos, audio, and head information</h2>
    <p>The app uses the camera and photos, videos, and image materials you select to capture, edit, add image or 3D stickers, and save creations. It also uses the microphone if you allow recording with audio.</p>
    <p>Photo and video processing and estimation of head position and orientation run on your device. The app does not send these photos, videos, audio, head positions, or angles to the Operator’s servers or include them in advertising requests.</p>
    <p>When you choose to share a creation, the app passes it to the app you select. The receiving service’s privacy policy applies to its handling of that content.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="section-3">
    <h2 id="section-3">3. Information stored on your device</h2>
    <p>The app stores settings, favorites, imported materials, editing drafts, information for restoring unfinished edits, face coverage review records and images, and information used to limit how often ads appear.</p>
    <p>Copies of photos, materials, person positions, and adjustments needed for drafts or edit recovery may be stored in the app’s private storage. These copies stay on your device.</p>
    <p>Rendered preview images are stored temporarily in the app’s private cache. Older temporary files are cleaned up during later review operations and can also be removed by clearing the app cache in Android settings.</p>
    <p>Exported creations are saved to your device’s media storage or a destination you choose.</p>
    <p>You can remove app information using available material deletion actions, by clearing app data in Android settings, or by uninstalling the app. Exported, copied, or shared files remain separately and must be deleted from their destinations when needed.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="section-4">
    <h2 id="section-4">4. Advertising services</h2>
    <p>The app uses Google Mobile Ads SDK (AdMob) and User Messaging Platform (UMP) SDK for consent management.</p>
    <p>Google’s SDKs may collect and share IP addresses, approximate location inferred from IP addresses, interactions with ads or the app, diagnostics such as launch time or hangs, and identifiers such as advertising ID and app set ID. These may be used for advertising, analytics, and fraud prevention. Handling varies with device settings, region, consent status, and Google’s services.</p>
    <p>The app requests non-personalized ads. This does not stop all data collection or sharing. User data collected by Google Mobile Ads SDK is encrypted in transit using TLS.</p>
    <p><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a></p>
    <p><a href="https://developers.google.com/admob/android/privacy/play-data-disclosure">Advertising SDK data disclosure</a></p>
    <p><a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/">Google ad controls</a></p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="section-5">
    <h2 id="section-5">5. Permissions and privacy choices</h2>
    <p>You can change camera and microphone permissions in Android settings.</p>
    <p>A consent form is shown where required by the consent management service. When Google’s consent management indicates that privacy options are required, you can change your choices under “Ads and privacy” in the app.</p>
    <p>Advertising ID settings can be reviewed and changed in the settings of supported Android devices.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="section-6">
    <h2 id="section-6">6. Retention and deletion requests</h2>
    <p>The Operator does not run servers that store the app’s photos, videos, audio, or head information. See section 3 for deleting information on your device. Retention and deletion of information collected by Google follow Google’s policies and available controls.</p>
    <p>If you contact support by email, your email address and message are used to respond and resolve the issue. This information is kept for as long as needed for that purpose and removed when no longer necessary. Contact the email address above for deletion inquiries.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="section-7">
    <h2 id="section-7">7. Age group</h2>
    <p>The app is intended for users aged 13 and over and is not directed at children under 13. Minors should consult a parent or guardian where appropriate.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="section-8">
    <h2 id="section-8">8. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>This policy may be updated as the app or its information handling changes. Updates will be posted on this page. Significant changes may also be announced in the app or through other appropriate means.</p>
  </section>
</KaburioPolicyLayout>

